 <a name="details" id="details"></a><h2 id="header-details" class="groupheader">Detailed Description</h2>
 <div class="textblock"><p>The class used to define a standard web page. </p>
-<p>Populate the _head property with any data needed there(title is already set) and fill <em>_children</em>  with the page's contents. </p>
+<p>Populate the _head property with any data needed there(title is already set) and fill <em>_children</em>  with the page's contents. When making your own page by extending this class, do the following:</p><ul>
+<li>Name your class the path excluding slashes, after slashes capitalise the letter, e.g. <code>/foo/bar/bazz/buzz</code> =&gt; <code>FooBarBazzBuzz</code></li>
+<li>Make a constructor as follows: <div class="fragment"><div class="line"><span class="keyword">public</span> FooBar() : base(</div>
+<div class="line">    new List&lt;<a class="code hl_interface" href="interfaceCFlat_1_1Html_1_1HtmlElement.html">HtmlElement</a>&gt;(),</div>
+<div class="line">    new <a class="code hl_class" href="classCFlat_1_1Html_1_1Attributes.html">Attributes</a>(),</div>
+<div class="line">    <span class="stringliteral">&quot;FooBar&quot;</span>,</div>
+<div class="line">    new <a class="code hl_class" href="classCFlat_1_1Html_1_1Base_1_1HtmlHead.html">HtmlHead</a>(new List&lt;<a class="code hl_class" href="classCFlat_1_1Html_1_1Base_1_1HtmlMeta.html">HtmlMeta</a>&gt;())</div>
+<div class="line">    )</div>
+<div class="line">{</div>
+<div class="line">    ...</div>
+<div class="line">}</div>
+<div class="ttc" id="aclassCFlat_1_1Html_1_1Attributes_html"><div class="ttname"><a href="classCFlat_1_1Html_1_1Attributes.html">CFlat.Html.Attributes</a></div><div class="ttdef"><b>Definition</b> Attributes.cs:57</div></div>
